hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19169","Qutayba ibn Said narrated to us: Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Zuhra ibn Mabad, from his grandfather, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he held the hand of Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him. So he said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, you are dearer to me than everything but myself. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in whose Hand is my soul, none of you believes until I am dearer to him than himself. He said: Then you are now, by Allah, dearer to me than myself. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Now, O Umar."
